entry.content:
apply_ifc_rules: description  +NOT NEEDED ON A MODEL ALREADY TREATED: when read_ifc_overview returns 'designation_existante', the units and fans are already designated - reuse them. Posting rules REPLACES that designation entirely: do it only when the user asks to start again, or when the designation plainly contradicts what they say. -TWO +THREE -and -ventilateur +ventilateur, and SMOKE EXHAUST fans - including fans that bring compensation air for smoke exhaust - the role ventilateur_desenfumage +A smoke fan runs only in a fire, with the ventilation stopped: a duct it shares with an air handling unit is not a plenum share
read_ifc_overview: description  +A MODEL ALREADY TREATED: if the answer carries 'designation_existante', an earlier session already designated the units and fans of this model. Reuse it: skip step 2, go straight to trace_duct_circuits, and show the user the designation you reused. Post new rules only if the user asks to start again. -and +and smoke exhaust fans (and smoke compensation fans) the role ventilateur_desenfumage,
trace_duct_circuits: description  +Never pick the units yourself, never go through them all in a row on your own, and never call in parallel (sub-agents, simultaneous calls): the calls on one model run one after the other on the server, and parallel calls only slow the site down for everyone. -one; +one the user asks for;
